First of all I want to say that I've been a fan of the franchise for almost 20 years now, I remember the first SS cd my father brought from Germany when I was 9, back in 2000.
Now let's talk about the game:
PROS:
Graphics;
Play style;
Sound effects/quality;
*Soundtrack;
*Campaign;
CONS:
Multiplayer (it's just bad, sorry);
Pathfinding;
*TOO FEW UNITS!!1!ONE!!;
A bit too Arcade-ish;
Well, my Pros/Cons list is very short and that is my intention, those are the main things I consider important in an RTS game.
*Soundtrack: I love how it adapts to specific moments inside the game, ie: when you approach enemy units a cool action-thrill music starts.
*Campaign: I feel it's a little shorter than it could be, but I'm enjoying it for what it is.
*Too few units: please, PLEASE give us more units to throw at our enemie's face!!!
That's all, this is way better than SS3 was, but it can still improve to become a reall SS title.
Keep up the hard work guys, well done!

